MATING-MATERIAL RERUN: RESPONSIBILITY v1.0.1
Build date: 2026-10-29

EXPECTED RUNTIME
5–15 minutes on the 12-core MacBook Pro with XT_Pro; allow 25 minutes on a
busy drive. The v1.0.0 reference fit took about 40 seconds before its comparison
guard stopped; a complete corrected production run is not yet measured.
The runner authenticates cached inputs, reproduces the 53 archived models,
then estimates the same 53 specifications on the corrected material frame.
It uses up to 10 workers, an 11 GB memory budget, one BLAS thread per worker,
and 32 whole-chooser shards. At least 4 GiB free on XT_Pro is required.
The installed five-package model environment is reused. Initial installation,
if needed, usually adds 1–3 minutes. RESOURCE_BENCHMARK.json documents the
synthetic compute benchmark; it is not a measurement on the user's Mac.

RUN FROM A FRESH TERMINAL
Save the ZIP and its .sha256 in ~/Desktop/Lichess_Desktop, then run:

bash <<'BASH'
set -e
cd "$HOME/Desktop/Lichess_Desktop"
shasum -a 256 -c Mating_Material_Responsibility_v1_0_1.zip.sha256
unzip -oq Mating_Material_Responsibility_v1_0_1.zip
bash Mating_Material_Responsibility_v1_0_1/RUN_RESPONSIBILITY.command
BASH

The launcher first runs the local tests. To run tests alone, add --self-test.
For preflight authentication and census only, add --preflight-only.
To print the runtime estimate only, add --estimate-only.
Rerun the same command after an interruption: completed, hash-verified
chooser shards are reused. A completed run is verified without refitting.
Corrupt completed checkpoints stop the run; they are not silently accepted.

CHANGE FROM v1.0.0
The returned run reproduced every reported coefficient, SE, planned contrast,
profile, sample count and rank. One of 53 full covariance comparisons failed
the old entrywise relative tolerance (maximum absolute difference 8.31e-8).
The failed return did not include the actual matrix, so it cannot establish
which entry triggered the failure or whether the revised check passes on the
Mac. v1.0.1 checks each full covariance entry on its natural SE-product scale:
  abs(new_ij - archived_ij) <= 2e-8 + 2e-7 * archived_SE_i * archived_SE_j.
It also rejects nonfinite, asymmetric or materially negative-variance matrices.
This handles a covariance near zero between coefficients with large marginal
variances without weakening the separate coefficient, SE or contrast checks.
The old entrywise verdict and the worst scaled discrepancy are still reported.
Aggregate reference matrices and all compared tables are now included in the
return ZIP even if this guard stops again. No estimation equation, source
feature, sample rule, covariance estimator or paper-facing formula changes.

This version writes to a separate v101 run directory. It reuses the existing
engine features and environment, but repeats the short regressions and input
projection instead of migrating the failed v100 regression checkpoints.

SCOPE
This package refreshes the responsibility / deliberate-departure checks.
The original repaired A2 producer defines 53 specifications: late and all-stage
evaluation profiles, own-move and two/four-ply losses, clock and material
proxies, joint models, direct region interactions, three blunder thresholds,
the rating-gap/blunder outcomes, rating-state controls, cross-region
comparisons, and the low-loss/ample-clock sensitivity.

The original target consists of 260,863 opportunities from the frozen
20,000-account sample. The runner intersects these games with the reviewed
material-restricted main panel and replaces y with the corrected grant
indicator. It does not add accounts or replace removed games. It checks that
all retained board, rating, clock, time, speed and chooser fields reproduce the
frozen producer's values. Prior outcomes and all original files stay intact.
Removed and reclassified game records remain in the private output tree.

All original cutoffs, knots, controls, fixed effects, covariance formulas and
planned Holm families are retained. The solver demeans whole chooser histories,
retains singletons and never-granters under the original convention, detects
non-estimable contrasts, and exports the full coefficient covariance and
standardized-profile influence state. The compact paper table is an extraction
from the full original contrast inventory, not a new specification search.

Before accepting the new estimates, the runner fits the original frame and
compares all 53 models to the archived repaired results: row-set hashes,
sample sizes, ranks, coefficients, SEs, planned contrasts, adjusted profile
levels and their SEs, and full covariance matrices. This is a reproduction
check only; the paper-facing outputs come from the corrected material frame.

The 53 archived models did not include prior-disconnection-history models.
Those additional models are not added or reported as completed here.
Countdown, tenure/arena/repeat, and the IV families remain separately listed
in DOWNSTREAM_STATUS.csv. This is not completion of the whole paper rerun.

INPUTS ALREADY ON THE MAC
Project root: __PRIVATE_VALUE_1__

1. Reviewed material-ready manifest:
   derived/replication/mating_material_first_run_v100_PRIVATE/
   aa7e95f275c18f43/MATERIAL_RESTRICTED_INPUTS_READY_PRIVATE.json
   Its completion receipt, reviewed hashes, 24 monthly main Parquets, and
   full main census are validated. The old missing author-exclusion-ready
   manifest is not an input to this package.

2. Original frozen target:
   output/tenure_responsibility_v100/c539ba215e708b22/
   PRIVATE/trajectory_targets.parquet
   SHA-256:
   a1b68dc9bdaf2d9a95494b9ec020ede0bcf75bd6fefcf340ba1e2b55ee5eba12

3. Repaired A2 features and their producer receipts:
   output/kac_a2_score_repair_v101/14eda066d25b14f4/
   PRIVATE/projected/*.parquet
   PRIVATE/overlay_shards/*.parquet
   report/*
   The frozen target hash, reviewed report hashes, exact unit membership,
   overlay hashes and reconstructed projection receipt keys are checked.

These inputs are reused read-only. No new engine searches, game downloads,
profile queries, or rating replay are performed. The engine and chess Python
package are not required: only the original target preparation, constants,
designs, estimator and reporting functions are executed. Full source files are
vendored byte-for-byte; the unused acquisition routines are never imported.

OUTPUTS
Private run root:
  __PRIVATE_VALUE_1__/derived/replication/
  mating_material_responsibility_v101_PRIVATE/<run hash>/

Return these three files from ~/Desktop/Lichess_Desktop:
  MATERIAL_RESPONSIBILITY_<run hash>_RESPONSIBILITY_READY.zip
  MATERIAL_RESPONSIBILITY_<run hash>_RESPONSIBILITY_READY.zip.sha256
  MATERIAL_RESPONSIBILITY_LATEST_PRIVATE.json

The return ZIP contains aggregate results, code, lineage, checksums and a log.
It excludes game rows, chooser identifiers, replays, source caches and profiles.
Key tables include tab_app_responsibility.csv, planned_contrasts.csv,
coefficients.csv, adjusted_profiles.csv, responsibility_region_interactions.csv,
SAMPLE_RECONCILIATION.csv, REFERENCE_REPRODUCTION.csv and model_samples.csv.
RESPONSIBILITY_BEFORE_AFTER.csv gives descriptive changes, with no invented
paired standard error for estimates from different frames.

VALIDATION
24 tests cover the reviewed material contract, frozen source/specification
identity, short-game missing endpoints, sample removal and label reconciliation,
projection and author exclusion, feature receipt lineage, independent explicit
chooser-dummy OLS and cluster-influence calculations, all 53 sharded fits versus
whole-frame moments, resumable checkpoints, corruption rejection, reporting,
wrapper completion/resume, and return-ZIP hashes and privacy gates. Two new
tests exercise near-zero covariance comparisons and reject changed correlations,
changed variances, nonfinite entries, asymmetry, and wrong matrix dimensions.

Python 3.11–3.13. Dependencies: numpy 2.3.5, pandas 2.3.3, pyarrow 20.0.0,
duckdb 1.3.2, scipy 1.16.3. Default environment:
  ~/Desktop/Lichess_Desktop/MatingMaterial_Models_Env_v100
MMR_PYTHON can name an existing supported Python interpreter.
MMRESPONSIBILITY_ENV can name a different isolated environment.
Optional flags: --project-root, --results-dir, --manifest, --workers,
--memory-gb, --hash-workers, --shards. Changing shards creates a new run identity.
